Units — This Trips Up Everyone
Speed is usually asked in km/hr, but time is often in seconds, distance in meters. 
Converting correctly is where most silly mistakes happen.

Conversion formulae (memorize these cold):
1] x km/hr = x * 5/18 m/s
2] x m/s = x * 18/5 km/hr
Where this comes from (so you never forget it): 1 km = 1000 m, 1 hr = 3600 s.
So 1 km/hr = 1000/3600 m/s = 5/18 m/s. Derive it once, and you'll never need to "remember" it again.
