##Relative Speed — The Big One

This is what 70% of TSD problems actually test.

1] Same direction (chasing):
                        [Relative Speed= S1 - S2]

2] Opposite direction (approaching/crossing each other):
                         [Relative Speed = S1 + S2]

Intuition: if two people run toward each other, the gap closes faster (speeds add). If one chases another,
the gap closes slower (speeds subtract) — makes sense since a faster car catching a slower one ahead 
only gains ground at the difference in their speeds                        
