## Special Case: Trains

Trains introduce one twist — the train's own length matters, because "crossing" something means the entire
train must pass it, nose to tail.

Train crossing a stationary point/pole/man: Distance = length of train
Train crossing a platform/bridge: Distance = length of train + length of platform
Train crossing another moving train: Distance = sum of both train lengths, using relative speed
(add/subtract speeds based on direction)
